From dbf8ea21edea38fc78f1a83cd80912bad201edc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:00:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [depends] libdvdread 7.1.1, libdvdcss 1.6.0

libdvdread 7.0.1 -> 7.1.1 and libdvdcss 1.5.0 -> 1.6.0. libdvdnav stays at
7.0.0, its latest release, and builds against the new libdvdread as it is.

The version files now name the archives VideoLAN publishes (.tar.xz, with
their SHA512 and where they are), as there is no mirrored copy of these
versions to name. A build that passes LIBDVDREAD_URL, LIBDVDCSS_URL and
their hashes, as LibreELEC does, takes only the version and the name of the
archive from these files.

libdvdread/01-all-disableopendir.patch is ported. libdvdread 7.1 reaches
files and directories through a table of functions (dvd_reader_filesystem_h,
src/file/file_posix.c), and findDirFile() lists the directory with
dir_open()/dir_read() to find a file whatever the case of its name. Kodi
links these libraries with its C library wrapper, so the path given to
dvdnav_open2() can be any path Kodi can read and every stat(), open() and
opendir() on it lands in Kodi's file system layer. With _XBMC, findDirFile()
has never listed the directory: it builds the path of the file with the
name as asked and returns whether stat() finds it. The port keeps exactly
that, through fs->stat(), which is how libdvdread now does every other
stat. As before, a file whose name is in another case is not found, save
for the VIDEO_TS/video_ts directory that findDVDFile() tries itself.

libdvdread/02-all-disablesymlink.patch and
libdvdcss/01-all-libc_read_improvement.patch only get their line numbers
right: they applied with an offset.

Not ported: the patches for Windows and for darwin_embedded, which can be
neither built nor tested on Linux and are left as they were. Tried on the
new sources: libdvdread 03, 04 and 05 no longer apply (the code they change
moved to src/file/file_win32.c or is gone), 06 and 08 are upstream;
libdvdcss 03 no longer applies (win2k_open() changed), 04 applies with an
offset, and 02 fails in meson.build, as it already did on 1.5.0, and in two
hunks of ioctl.c. 07-emscripten-bswap.patch applies as it is.
